00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.940
Salad Fingers,  Don't Hug Me I'm Scared

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.860
and today we welcome another member into the hallowed halls of weird YouTube channels

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.600
that will haunt your dreams

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.060
but instead of me saying anything, I'll 
just let her introduce herself.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.060
She's quite good at it.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:05.800
"I'm Poppy"

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.740
"I'm Poppy"

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.740
"Poppy" *repeats*

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:09.480
"I'm Poppy"

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.980
"Pop" *repeats*

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.980
Alright! Alright! Enough! We get it. Point taken.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.500
In case you haven't seen this channel 
on either Pewds or Fine Bros.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.500
Let me introduce you to "Poppy,"

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.760
an aspiring singer who has both a 
Vevo channel for her original songs

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.340
and a personal channel where she 
posts frequent short videos of herself

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.900
and you might think that this sounds 
perfectly straightforward

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.000
and wonder why this would EVER, EVER merit a Film Theory,™

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.080
Instead of, say, I don't know, a third 
part of Doctor Who.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.320
Well, it's because the content of the 
videos on her personal channel

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.500
are... a bit more than what they appear.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.260
Sure! She might inflate and deflate a rabbit toy over and over again

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.260
or cryptically talk about what time it is

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:52.380
or just read the Bible straight from the beginning for a solid 49 minutes

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.200
and at first glance you might be thinking that

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.960
Poppy's videos are just random for the sake of being random.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.460
There are plenty of other channels on YouTube guilty of exactly that.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.220
But Poppy's aren't.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:06.040
I've gone through every one of that Poppy's videos,

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.100
and there are a BUNCH of them.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.100
As well as all her social feeds and

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.100
websites, and there is definitely

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.480
a much more sinister narrative going on here.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.480
Poppy, and the other people behind these videos,

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.480
most notably, their director, named

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.480
Titanic Sinclair, yes,

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.480
you heard me right, his name is Titanic

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.480
Sinclair like the boat and

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.480
the author of the most famous muckraking novel

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.480
of all time, The Jungle, Upton Sinclair,

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.480
are using these videos to comment on what it takes

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.480
to be a pop star in the modern age.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.480
And I don't mean struggling your way through the ranks

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.480
from humble beginnings,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.480
I mean being churned out by a cold

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.320
corporate machine and selling your soul

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.560
to the Illuminati™.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.000
You heard that right.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.280
Poppy equals

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.480
Illuminati, confirmed! Now that might

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.480
sound like a far-fetched conclusion to draw,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.480
but the evidence is there.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.480
So, strap in everybody, because the

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.480
road to hell is paved in pastel

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.480
pinks, has a really catchy reggae

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.980
beat and occurs in four

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:58.940
quick phases.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.260
Phase Number One:

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.020
Innocent, but sexual.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.480
One of the first things you'll notice about Poppy is that she appears

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.440
very young,

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.700
but how old is she really?

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.040
Is she around sixteen?

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.360
Or maybe she's just a

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:11.860
young looking twenty-something?

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.480
It's hard to tell and the people behind the channel are

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.920
certainly interested in keeping her age a secret.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.480
As Poppy said in an interview

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.480
with 'Racked.com', quote,

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.720
"I don't want people to talk about how old I am;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.480
I want to talk about what I'm making."

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.480
Either way, the clues to Poppy's youth are

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.980
everywhere in her early videos.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.880
Her very first video shows her eating cotton candy.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.480
In another, she's playing

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.880
'He Loves Me, He Loves Me Not' with a flower.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.480
Yet another shows her hula hooping

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.480
and the name of her first extended play is

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.480
called 'Bubble Bath'. These choices

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.480
are clearly no accident, because when asked in an

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.140
interview to describe her style in three words,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.160
Poppy states,

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.020
"Barbie, Kawaii, Child."

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.480
Barbie explains the pink clothes and blonde hair

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.880
and Kawaii, the Japanese concept of cuteness,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.980
exemplified by things like Hello Kitty™,

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.480
is also pretty obvious.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.480
One look at her music video for 'Money' and you see

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.480
that Japanese aesthetic everywhere, but

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.480
Child is the important one,

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.480
because it connects her to so many young blonde

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:07.600
pop stars that we've seen over the 
past twenty years.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.260
For comparison, consider Britney Spears.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.480
We're all probably somewhat

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.480
familiar with 21st century Britney,

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.480
the one who wore a snake to the BMAs,

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.800
made-out with Madonna and shaved her head,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.800
but I'm sure that those of you who can't tell a

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.800
jennxpenn from an RclBeauty can

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.800
also remember late 90s Britney as

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.180
well, when she first hit the scene.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.800
In the video for her first major hit, 
'...Baby One More Time',

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.800
Spears' teenage-ness is

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.800
on blatant display through her Catholic school

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.800
girl outfit, which, of course, comes with

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.800
plenty of sexualization on it's own.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.800
I mean, I've been invited to Catholic 
school dances before,

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.800
and I have seen some pretty wild

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.800
things at them, but those moves

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.400
that Britney's doing aren't leaving any room for Jesus.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.800
Now, in those early days, she was

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.800
an undeniable sex symbol,

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.800
but in interviews would outright

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.200
deny it, telling Esquire in 2003

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:51.960
that, quote,

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.460
"Look, if you want me to be some kind 
of sex thing, that's not me."

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:56.800
Are you sure, Britney?

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.000
Because she said this to a magazine that ran pictures

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.000
like this of her next to

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.000
the very same interview!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.400
Yeah, 'cuz all the innocent girls I know 
are are doing photo shoots

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.400
topless, pulling down their

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.380
panties and covering up their private parts

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.380
with giant strands of pearls!

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.860
What did you think those pictures were for?

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:16.160
*mocking Britney*
"It's not sexual, it's just artwork"

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.320
DEAR BRITNEY,

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.280
when the lyrics to your big song outright say

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.960
"I'm not that innocent,"

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:23.800
forgive people

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.800
for being a little skeptical

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.020
when you say that you

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:29.340
"are so innocent."

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.940
That is ALL I'm saying.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.800
But back to 2017.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.800
It's hard to deny that Poppy is drawing

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.200
some parallels here.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.800
Just compare this still of Poppy from the video

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.800
where she introduces herself to the cover

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.800
of Britney Spears' first album.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.800
Poppy also expresses the same kind of

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.000
aversion to sexuality as early era

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.660
Britney did, albeit in subtler ways.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.000
Take a moment from the video

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.000
for Poppy's biggest single 'Lowlife.'

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.000
She's seated at a table with the devil,

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.000
more on that one later, who peels a banana,

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.000
puts it in his mouth, and, um,

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.600
doesn't start to eat it.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.480
That, sir, is a choking hazard, Mr. Satan.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.500
Didn't anyone ever tell you to chew your food?

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.000
Sure, we don't see anything 
particularly graphic going on here,

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.000
but Poppy's reaction tells us pretty much

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.480
everything that we need to know.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.000
Sex is not a part of Poppy or her message,

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.400
but the companies that manage, publicize,

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.960
and basically create popstars

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.880
don't care what your message is.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:21.520
In the words of another pop star,

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.680
Pink, and her song "Don't Let Me Get Me,"

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:26.360
quote, "LA told me, you'll be a pop star.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.200
All you have to change is everything you are."

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.440
They want their stars to be sexually appealing

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:32.780
because it gets them attention

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.040
and helps them sell to adults,

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.880
whilst still staying innocuous enough

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.820
that parents don't find them too harmful

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:38.980
for the younger fans.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.420
And if they're able to pull of this balancing act,

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.180
that leads them to

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.060
Phase 2:

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.880
Dallah, Dallah bills.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.340
Admittedly , this is the most self-explanatory of the phases,

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.740
but it's one that the creators of the Poppy channel

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.820
definitely want to acknowledge in their story.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.000
The first indication of money that we get

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.900
is in the video, "I made 500 dollars."

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.860
In which, Poppy gleefully examines

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.620
and counts a stack of five 100 dollar bills she received.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.160
How she earned that money isn't 
entirely clear though

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.340
perhaps, it's the result of the video titled,

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:07.040
"Tide Commercial,"

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.160
in which Poppy declares her love for Tide

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.740
and talks about how much better her life is

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.120
as a result of the detergent.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.520
But even more egregious than that is the song, "Money,"

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.600
which shamelessly promotes

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.260
materialism with lyrics like,

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:22.080
"If money can't buy happiness then 
why is it so fabulous?"

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.680
You can draw parallels to pop music here,

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:24.700
but it's pretty obvious

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.460
"With fame, comes money."

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.000
But, of course, with fame and money

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.320
there come some drawbacks

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:30.700
and that takes us to

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.480
Phase 3:

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.180
Losing control of your message.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.220
If there's one way to make

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.940
your fan base turn on you is becoming a

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:36.880
#

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:37.380
#Sellout

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:37.900
&gt;:(

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.040
Once the celebrity gets hot,

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.180
their list of responsibility goes way beyond

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:42.380
just making music.

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.520
At one point, Lady Gaga considered quitting

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.780
music all together citing that she was unhappy

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.960
with a variety of things but especially

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.240
being used to make other people money

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.200
by doing things like selling fragrances

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.200
or standing around taking pictures.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.840
When she stopped doing those things,

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.440
she says she remembered who she was.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:00.440
As though taking away everything behind the scenes

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.300
restored her individuality.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.580
Similarly, there are outside forces that try

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.800
to control what Poppy has to say in a lot of her videos

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.520
In "Lowlife," the first music video I talked about earlier,

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.560
we see men in suits in breathing 
masks and wheelchairs.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:16.300
The men behind the scenes, pulling the strings

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.040
and trying to get Poppy to sell out.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.560
The devil, and his, um,

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:20.260
banana.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.900
Poppy in this video is able to reject their control,

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.680
as shown by her shoving them off-stage

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.940
but fast-forward to more recent videos,

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.940
and this tide is starting to change

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.600
In the video titled, "Shirt,"

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.080
Poppy is holding a t-shirt containing her lyric,

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.480
"If money can't buy happiness then why is it so fabulous?"

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.300
Poppy looks off camera and asks,

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.720
"What do you want me to say?"

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.980
The answer we get is garble and mechanical

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:43.020
(garbled mechanical audio)

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:46.640
but if you alter the pitch using audio manipulation tools,

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:47.620
you get this:

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.780
"Just read what is on the shirt."

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.900
Just read what's on the shirt.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.460
At which point, Poppy reads the slogan.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:56.240
Later in the video, the voice tells Poppy

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.040
to tell the people to buy the t-shirts.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.440
"Tell them to buy the t-shirt."

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.060
And she complies again.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.960
This represent the time recently

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.340
after a pop star becomes famous

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.640
and is being pushed around doing sale

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.120
promote everything that other people wants.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.060
In a more recent video called, "I'm Not Lying To You,"

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:15.540
we get another crypted message from a skull

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.440
that speaks to Poppy in reverse,

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.580
*DEMONIC VOICE*

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:20.780
Decoded, it says,

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.900
"The next word I'm going to say is yes,"

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:24.500
but only before, this time,

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.360
Poppy doesn't follow instructions claiming that,

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:30.000
"I used to be more honest but now they won't let me."

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.200
In fact, Poppy makes a lot of references

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.900
to an unseen but powerful

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:34.520
"THEY,"

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:35.680
in many of her videos

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.680
so, who are "They,"?

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.100
Are "They" the businessmen

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.320
who we saw on set with her?

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.000
Well,

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:41.500
yes,

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:44.260
but it's also far more dangerous than that.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.500
And here's when things start to go off the rail.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.680
In "Japan", we get the typical Poppy-esq

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:49.780
statements like,

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:52.500
"What is the difference between Hollywood and Japan?"

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.180
and,

